1
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:43,439
Fuck!

2
00:01:51,716 --> 00:01:54,510
Fuck, I'm already hungry again.

3
00:01:56,429 --> 00:01:58,473
The meal was expensive as hell too.

4
00:02:44,519 --> 00:02:47,522
MOUSETRAP

5
00:02:58,032 --> 00:03:00,535
Shouldn't we have gone back to that place?

6
00:03:01,411 --> 00:03:02,370
He was there.

7
00:03:02,453 --> 00:03:04,747
As if he'd still be there. Fuck.

8
00:03:05,373 --> 00:03:07,959
Besides, those hit men?
They were after me.

9
00:03:08,042 --> 00:03:09,085
Who were they?

10
00:03:09,168 --> 00:03:10,461
None of your business, punk.

11
00:03:10,545 --> 00:03:13,214
Shit. This is getting out of fucking hand.

12
00:03:13,298 --> 00:03:15,842
But how the hell did he know
where we were?

13
00:03:15,925 --> 00:03:17,552
He knew we were at the motel too.

14
00:03:18,052 --> 00:03:19,637
I even threw away my phone.

15
00:03:20,221 --> 00:03:21,514
Who knows?

16
00:03:22,724 --> 00:03:23,808
Maybe he's tailing us.

17
00:03:27,603 --> 00:03:29,605
Fuck! Every time I get involved with you,

18
00:03:29,689 --> 00:03:32,025
my life goes to total shit!

19
00:03:32,525 --> 00:03:35,820
Once I get my fucking money back,
don't ever come near me. Got it?

20
00:03:38,823 --> 00:03:40,867
Hey, fuck, which island is it?

21
00:03:45,413 --> 00:03:47,373
That bastard will be there for sure.

22
00:03:47,874 --> 00:03:49,167
At least a trace of him.

23
00:03:54,297 --> 00:03:56,507
They were brought in on a restaurant call?

24
00:03:56,591 --> 00:03:58,885
Both unidentified persons?

25
00:03:58,968 --> 00:04:00,511
Yes, that's right.

26
00:04:00,595 --> 00:04:01,512
Oh man.

27
00:04:02,013 --> 00:04:04,640
What's this world fucking coming to?

28
00:04:05,683 --> 00:04:08,644
Jesus, his jaw's totally smashed.

29
00:04:09,312 --> 00:04:11,022
I know how that feels.

30
00:04:11,105 --> 00:04:11,981
Hey!

31
00:04:12,565 --> 00:04:14,901
The nurses say you speak some Korean.

32
00:04:14,984 --> 00:04:17,528
That bastard's not talking. You talk.

33
00:04:17,612 --> 00:04:21,949
Why are you both unidentified persons?
How do you end up like that, huh?

34
00:04:23,826 --> 00:04:24,786
Are you sleeping?

35
00:04:25,495 --> 00:04:27,538
This bastard's eyelids are twitching.

36
00:04:31,250 --> 00:04:33,294
Hey, where's Noja?

37
00:04:33,795 --> 00:04:36,047
Just tell me, and I'll leave you alone.

38
00:04:41,427 --> 00:04:43,638
You got into an argument
in the parking lot.

39
00:04:43,721 --> 00:04:47,016
And then he just started
beating the shit out of you.

40
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:50,019
So you guys are basically just victims.

41
00:04:50,103 --> 00:04:51,020
Right?

42
00:04:51,104 --> 00:04:53,064
Damn, you must be so upset.

43
00:04:56,317 --> 00:04:58,694
Is that how you want it in the report?

44
00:05:21,008 --> 00:05:22,760
What the hell is going on?

45
00:05:24,178 --> 00:05:26,431
Whatever the hell is going on,

46
00:05:26,514 --> 00:05:28,641
why are we handling this?

47
00:05:28,724 --> 00:05:29,892
Why not Violent Crimes?

48
00:05:29,976 --> 00:05:32,603
We've got a shit ton of work
to do already.

49
00:05:32,687 --> 00:05:35,022
Man, what a headache.

50
00:05:35,106 --> 00:05:36,941
That tip's killing us.

51
00:05:37,692 --> 00:05:39,235
Find this guy first.

52
00:05:39,318 --> 00:05:41,070
He runs an identity fraud ring.

53
00:05:44,115 --> 00:05:47,410
Catch him and lean on him.
You're probably looking at a promotion.

54
00:05:54,584 --> 00:05:56,461
What are you doing? Aren't you gonna go?

55
00:05:57,462 --> 00:05:58,880
Hurry up. Go get him.

56
00:06:00,006 --> 00:06:01,424
You think you're in charge?

57
00:06:01,507 --> 00:06:04,427
No one's in charge here.
We're all just fucking grunts.

58
00:06:05,636 --> 00:06:06,637
Where are you going?

59
00:06:07,263 --> 00:06:08,890
I'm going to work.

60
00:06:08,973 --> 00:06:10,558
That little…

61
00:06:13,060 --> 00:06:14,228
Come on, sir.

62
00:06:14,312 --> 00:06:16,063
Why not send him to Violent Crimes?

63
00:06:16,147 --> 00:06:18,191
He freaking loves those cases.

64
00:06:18,691 --> 00:06:20,985
It's you who's got
the Violent Crimes look.

65
00:06:21,986 --> 00:06:23,196
Damn it.

66
00:06:30,203 --> 00:06:32,872
Come on. Let's go!

67
00:06:35,291 --> 00:06:36,167
Hey.

68
00:06:37,877 --> 00:06:41,631
Can't a cop enjoy his fucking hobby
on his day off? Huh?

69
00:06:41,714 --> 00:06:43,799
This place isn't illegal!

70
00:06:44,759 --> 00:06:46,802
Huh? What's with your face?

71
00:06:47,470 --> 00:06:50,097
Is this place illegal?

72
00:06:50,973 --> 00:06:52,934
Hey. Go get the owner.

73
00:06:53,768 --> 00:06:55,102
What's the owner's name?

74
00:06:55,603 --> 00:06:58,105
I said go get the owner!

75
00:06:58,189 --> 00:07:01,567
Yes, I'm Kang Myeong-su.
What seems to be the problem?

76
00:07:04,946 --> 00:07:06,614
-Kang Myeong-su?
-Yes.

77
00:07:08,741 --> 00:07:10,243
Kang Myeong-su?

78
00:07:12,370 --> 00:07:14,997
You look familiar,
but the name doesn't ring a bell.

79
00:07:15,081 --> 00:07:16,499
Have we met?

80
00:07:18,584 --> 00:07:19,710
I don't think so.

81
00:07:19,794 --> 00:07:20,920
Really?

82
00:07:23,130 --> 00:07:24,215
So,

83
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:27,134
you don't have Go-Stop here?

84
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:30,555
Well, what do you want?

85
00:07:30,638 --> 00:07:32,014
Right.

86
00:07:39,897 --> 00:07:42,525
We could come by every day. Okay?

87
00:07:42,608 --> 00:07:46,612
We've got all the fucking time
in the world. Okay?

88
00:08:03,671 --> 00:08:05,464
Doesn't look like he'll last the week.

89
00:08:05,548 --> 00:08:07,675
-Terminal liver cancer?
-Yes, sir.

90
00:08:07,758 --> 00:08:10,136
-Where did you find him?
-A homeless shelter.

91
00:08:10,219 --> 00:08:11,887
I laundered his identity clean.

92
00:08:16,892 --> 00:08:18,811
He was born in Korea,

93
00:08:18,894 --> 00:08:21,731
and now he's dying as an illegal alien.

94
00:08:26,444 --> 00:08:27,320
Hey, Myeong-su.

95
00:08:27,403 --> 00:08:28,988
Hey, the cops were just here.

96
00:08:29,071 --> 00:08:30,156
Yeah?

97
00:08:30,656 --> 00:08:32,158
That's nothing new.

98
00:08:32,241 --> 00:08:34,118
They won't get a warrant. No evidence.

99
00:08:34,201 --> 00:08:35,536
They were looking for you.

100
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:36,996
Don't come here.

101
00:08:37,079 --> 00:08:38,289
I'll handle it somehow.

102
00:08:38,372 --> 00:08:40,666
Noja, that son of a bitch.

103
00:08:40,750 --> 00:08:43,002
He's gonna fuck us all up.

104
00:08:43,502 --> 00:08:46,922
Why the hell did you send those morons?
Now it's a bigger mess!

105
00:08:47,006 --> 00:08:49,342
You couldn't find someone
who could do it right?

106
00:08:50,051 --> 00:08:52,136
For fuck's sake. Forget it! I'll do it.

107
00:08:52,219 --> 00:08:53,971
You just handle the site, okay?

108
00:08:56,474 --> 00:08:58,476
This fucking bastard.

109
00:08:59,935 --> 00:09:01,687
Seriously, this fucking bastard.

110
00:09:02,355 --> 00:09:03,814
Man, this fucking dumbass.

111
00:09:03,898 --> 00:09:06,567
He's so fucking useless. For fuck's sake.

112
00:09:10,613 --> 00:09:11,656
A business trip?

113
00:09:11,739 --> 00:09:13,199
I'll go get him real quick.

114
00:09:16,118 --> 00:09:17,745
You told me to go start a fire.

115
00:09:17,828 --> 00:09:19,580
I did, but he still hasn't come out.

116
00:09:19,664 --> 00:09:22,291
He will if you keep it up.
Those two are in it together.

117
00:09:22,833 --> 00:09:25,252
Hey! You dumping the legwork on us?

118
00:09:25,336 --> 00:09:28,005
Looks like that gut
could use some legwork, asshole.

119
00:09:29,423 --> 00:09:30,716
Take Chang-u or Min-ho.

120
00:09:30,800 --> 00:09:32,176
I'm putting someone on you.

121
00:09:32,259 --> 00:09:34,220
I prefer working alone.

122
00:09:34,762 --> 00:09:37,306
Yeah. I prefer working alone too.

123
00:09:37,390 --> 00:09:38,474
You can take them all.

124
00:09:38,557 --> 00:09:40,810
Come on, sir. I prefer working alone too.

125
00:09:40,893 --> 00:09:41,769
Damn it.

126
00:09:41,852 --> 00:09:43,187
Hey, kid. Follow me.

127
00:09:43,270 --> 00:09:44,355
Why?

128
00:09:44,438 --> 00:09:47,108
"Why?" Y comes after X, you bastard.

129
00:09:47,858 --> 00:09:50,528
Look at him taking his sweet time.
He's just strolling.

130
00:09:50,611 --> 00:09:51,654
That bastard.

131
00:09:56,450 --> 00:09:57,785
Where are we going?

132
00:10:00,121 --> 00:10:02,665
-When was the last time you saw the ocean?
-What?

133
00:10:02,748 --> 00:10:04,750
The ocean, you bastard.

134
00:11:08,022 --> 00:11:11,859
If this is his parents' restaurant,
that lady must be his mom.

135
00:11:11,942 --> 00:11:12,777
Right?

136
00:11:14,403 --> 00:11:15,946
Stay out of this. I'll handle it.

137
00:11:18,157 --> 00:11:19,200
You look too…

138
00:11:29,251 --> 00:11:30,336
You're not?

139
00:11:30,419 --> 00:11:33,798
Oh, I'm just the new owner here.

140
00:11:34,632 --> 00:11:38,636
I know the previous owner well.
We lived in the same neighborhood.

141
00:11:39,553 --> 00:11:43,682
Oh my, he went through a lot
because of that troublemaker son of his.

142
00:11:43,766 --> 00:11:46,727
I mean, he didn't even visit
when his father died.

143
00:11:47,311 --> 00:11:51,482
He only showed up briefly
when I was taking over the shop.

144
00:11:51,565 --> 00:11:52,942
Just to collect the money.

145
00:11:53,526 --> 00:11:55,486
So when was that…

146
00:11:56,821 --> 00:12:01,116
That was maybe three or four years ago.

147
00:12:02,368 --> 00:12:05,037
Oh, go to the harbor. His friend's there.

148
00:12:22,638 --> 00:12:23,514
Hey!

149
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:27,518
Hey!

150
00:12:28,769 --> 00:12:30,145
Do you know Seo Yu-min?

151
00:12:33,607 --> 00:12:34,608
Yu-min?

152
00:12:34,692 --> 00:12:35,651
Yes.

153
00:12:39,572 --> 00:12:40,739
What about that bastard?

154
00:12:41,866 --> 00:12:43,617
Well, you see--

155
00:12:43,701 --> 00:12:44,618
Hey.

156
00:12:47,413 --> 00:12:49,331
We're from Seoul.

157
00:12:54,295 --> 00:12:57,965
Our squad leader may not sound like it,
but he really cares about you.

158
00:12:58,757 --> 00:13:00,801
Just tell him to worry about himself.

159
00:13:01,510 --> 00:13:02,887
You two go way back, right?

160
00:13:02,970 --> 00:13:06,015
Yeah, all the way back
to when he was dating his wife.

161
00:13:06,098 --> 00:13:09,184
That's about the same as us.

162
00:13:11,395 --> 00:13:12,229
Hey.

163
00:13:12,855 --> 00:13:15,566
He only turned out okay
because he met the right woman.

164
00:13:15,649 --> 00:13:17,318
That's why they're happy together.

165
00:13:17,401 --> 00:13:19,361
His wife deserves some credit,

166
00:13:19,445 --> 00:13:21,196
but he also treats her really well.

167
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:22,197
Very affectionate.

168
00:13:22,281 --> 00:13:25,242
Yeah. He doesn't break walls
like someone here.

169
00:13:25,326 --> 00:13:27,620
He's not facing a divorce either, right?

170
00:13:28,412 --> 00:13:30,623
Why are we back on that again?

171
00:13:32,750 --> 00:13:35,210
I'm just not cut out for family.

172
00:13:35,711 --> 00:13:37,463
I'm an orphan. Damn it.

173
00:13:37,546 --> 00:13:40,883
I don't even know
who my real parents are, you know?

174
00:13:40,966 --> 00:13:42,551
I was abandoned at an orphanage.

175
00:13:42,635 --> 00:13:45,596
Well, I was adopted.

176
00:13:46,430 --> 00:13:49,683
Fuck, I guess they didn't like me.
They sent me back.

177
00:13:50,267 --> 00:13:51,226
Huh?

178
00:13:51,310 --> 00:13:54,355
Back to the orphanage.
Adopted again, sent back again.

179
00:13:55,564 --> 00:13:57,858
-Kid.
-Sir?

180
00:13:58,359 --> 00:14:00,694
I'm just not meant to have a family.

181
00:14:03,739 --> 00:14:04,698
We're your family.

182
00:14:05,866 --> 00:14:07,326
Bullshit.

183
00:14:09,745 --> 00:14:12,998
Family, my ass. Once they turn away,
they're just strangers.

184
00:14:16,168 --> 00:14:19,880
In the end, we all live like islands.

185
00:14:48,283 --> 00:14:50,077
It's been a while. What a mess.

186
00:14:50,786 --> 00:14:52,204
This is Yu-min's place.

187
00:14:54,123 --> 00:14:56,542
Why are you looking for him?
Did he scam someone again?

188
00:14:56,625 --> 00:14:59,461
Oh, so he scammed someone around here too?

189
00:14:59,545 --> 00:15:01,964
He borrowed from everyone
and made a mess of things.

190
00:15:02,464 --> 00:15:03,298
Money again?

191
00:15:03,799 --> 00:15:05,426
Yeah, money. A lot of money.

192
00:15:05,509 --> 00:15:06,802
Figures.

193
00:15:06,885 --> 00:15:08,721
He hasn't been here for a long time.

194
00:15:08,804 --> 00:15:10,139
It sat empty for a while.

195
00:15:10,222 --> 00:15:12,599
Someone rented it
for a few months last year.

196
00:15:12,683 --> 00:15:15,978
He wasn't a fisherman.
I think he said he was a writer.

197
00:15:16,854 --> 00:15:18,522
Actually, he looked kinda like you--

198
00:15:18,605 --> 00:15:21,734
Well, I mean,
have you seen him since then?

199
00:15:23,027 --> 00:15:23,861
No.

200
00:15:24,445 --> 00:15:27,698
That bastard somehow
had a girl on his arm.

201
00:15:28,323 --> 00:15:29,158
A girl?

202
00:15:29,241 --> 00:15:31,410
Yeah, he showed up with some girl.

203
00:15:31,493 --> 00:15:34,246
They stayed here together
when they came down.

204
00:16:53,408 --> 00:16:55,577
Goddamn it. What the hell are you doing?

205
00:17:00,541 --> 00:17:01,542
What about his friend?

206
00:17:02,167 --> 00:17:03,252
He left!

207
00:17:03,335 --> 00:17:06,338
He doesn't have his number.
They haven't been in touch.

208
00:17:06,421 --> 00:17:07,422
So what now?

209
00:17:08,966 --> 00:17:12,094
Apparently, he's got stuff in the attic.
We should check it out.

210
00:17:12,928 --> 00:17:15,013
Weren't you fucking listening earlier?

211
00:17:16,265 --> 00:17:17,808
Damn it.

212
00:17:25,649 --> 00:17:27,067
Shit.

213
00:17:28,402 --> 00:17:31,196
Hey, I think that bastard Yu-min
is the rat bastard.

214
00:17:31,697 --> 00:17:34,283
If those two bastards aren't the same guy,

215
00:17:34,783 --> 00:17:36,660
how do their movements all lead

216
00:17:38,453 --> 00:17:40,205
to a house all the way out here?

217
00:17:50,924 --> 00:17:51,925
Hey, come here.

218
00:17:59,766 --> 00:18:01,476
Hey, this is the rat hole.

219
00:18:05,814 --> 00:18:07,316
Sheesh.

220
00:18:14,323 --> 00:18:16,742
He said he'd been preparing
for a long time.

221
00:18:16,825 --> 00:18:19,203
He even changed his face and voice

222
00:18:19,703 --> 00:18:21,747
to take everything you've got.

223
00:18:22,331 --> 00:18:23,832
Didn't I tell you?

224
00:18:24,333 --> 00:18:26,835
Everything was planned.

225
00:18:28,128 --> 00:18:31,048
The phone, the broken glass…

226
00:18:32,424 --> 00:18:35,010
Maybe even Da-eun's kidnapping.

227
00:19:27,229 --> 00:19:28,230
Hey, is this it?

228
00:19:29,147 --> 00:19:29,982
Huh?

229
00:19:31,149 --> 00:19:33,193
The stuff he was keeping here.

230
00:19:36,446 --> 00:19:37,906
Shit.

231
00:19:44,329 --> 00:19:45,580
What the hell?

232
00:19:46,164 --> 00:19:49,251
Who the hell parks this close to the edge?

233
00:19:49,334 --> 00:19:51,586
-I'm sorry.
-You trying to make me fall off?

234
00:19:54,715 --> 00:19:56,425
Hey, who do we ask?

235
00:19:56,508 --> 00:19:57,592
Hold on a sec.

236
00:20:00,846 --> 00:20:01,680
Oh.

237
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:04,141
Excuse me. We're with the police.

238
00:20:04,641 --> 00:20:07,602
We're looking for someone.

239
00:20:13,108 --> 00:20:14,443
Hey, Jeong-bae!

240
00:20:15,527 --> 00:20:17,029
Cops are here again.

241
00:20:21,783 --> 00:20:23,869
What does he mean by "again"?

242
00:20:26,872 --> 00:20:28,040
Hello.

243
00:20:28,623 --> 00:20:29,958
Mr. Jeong-bae!

244
00:20:30,751 --> 00:20:31,918
Are you Mr. Jeong-bae?

245
00:20:44,723 --> 00:20:46,016
What are those pictures?

246
00:20:48,435 --> 00:20:50,020
Good fucking times, huh?

247
00:20:56,276 --> 00:20:57,277
Wait.

248
00:20:58,570 --> 00:21:00,322
So this is that bastard Yu-min?

249
00:21:01,198 --> 00:21:02,032
Yeah.

250
00:21:02,741 --> 00:21:04,701
Shit. Are you sure?

251
00:21:09,581 --> 00:21:11,458
We really are all tangled up.

252
00:21:12,876 --> 00:21:14,336
I know this bastard too.

253
00:21:14,419 --> 00:21:15,796
How do you know Yu-min?

254
00:21:31,520 --> 00:21:32,354
You came?

255
00:21:32,938 --> 00:21:35,273
Punk, you just got home after two days?

256
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:38,151
I've spent a month looking for you.

257
00:21:38,652 --> 00:21:40,695
You borrowed money from a loan shark.

258
00:21:40,779 --> 00:21:44,074
Why does a kid like you
need money so badly?

259
00:21:45,534 --> 00:21:46,576
Have you eaten?

260
00:21:49,413 --> 00:21:50,247
Sit.

261
00:21:50,747 --> 00:21:53,333
I made two ramyeon.
Let's eat before we go.

262
00:21:57,796 --> 00:21:58,630
Go where?

263
00:21:59,756 --> 00:22:01,591
To the guy looking for you.

264
00:22:06,930 --> 00:22:08,390
You're not running away. Okay?

265
00:22:08,473 --> 00:22:11,017
It's cold out. Let's not make it harder.

266
00:22:12,853 --> 00:22:13,937
I'm not running away.

267
00:22:15,397 --> 00:22:16,898
If I can't pay it back,

268
00:22:17,941 --> 00:22:19,526
